## 1. Project Overview
KZN Collectibles & TCG is a hobbyist retail store operating in Pietermaritzburg and Hilton, KwaZulu-Natal. This web application provides a responsive product catalogue, interactive store location mapping, live inventory filtering, automated tournament seat/cost estimation, and client-side form validation.



## 2. Working Through Feedback from Part 2 (Fixes Implemented)
Following the lecturer's feedback from Part 2 stating that the code did not execute as expected during marking, a comprehensive technical audit and refactoring were completed:
1. Replaced Experimental CSS Selectors: Removed the `section:has(article)` selector from `css/styles.css` and implemented explicit, cross-browser compatible class selectors (`.card-grid`, `.product-card`, `.site-nav`). This ensures consistent rendering across all modern and legacy browsers (Grant, 2018: 74).
2. Standardised Relative File Paths: Verified that all five HTML files link accurately to `css/styles.css` and `js/scripts.js` using lowercase relative paths, preventing case-sensitivity failures when deployed to Linux-based hosting environments such as GitHub Pages (Duckett, 2014: 412).
3. Self-Healing Visual Assets: Implemented SEO-friendly image paths alongside inline SVG fallback data URIs so that visual elements and the Gallery Lightbox render reliably even in offline marking environments.



## 3. Part 3 JavaScript Enhancements & Functionality
In alignment with modern DOM manipulation standards (Flanagan, 2020: 389), the following interactive features were engineered in `js/scripts.js`:
Interactive Elements (Accordions & Tabs):** Implemented an accessible FAQ Accordion on `about.html` using `aria-expanded` attributes and dynamic height transitions, alongside interactive format tabs on `index.html` (MDN Web Docs, 2026a).
Interactive Maps (Leaflet.js Integration):** Integrated the open-source Leaflet.js mapping library on `contact.html` displaying interactive pins, popups, and branch-switching controls for both the Pietermaritzburg Flagship Store (`-29.6006, 30.3794`) and the Hilton Express Outlet (`-29.5547, 30.3014`) (Leaflet, 2026).
Responsive Gallery Lightbox:** Built a custom modal lightbox across `index.html` and `products.html` supporting click-to-zoom, dynamic captions, next/previous navigation, and keyboard accessibility (`Escape`, `ArrowLeft`, `ArrowRight`).
Dynamic Content, Live Search, Filtering & Sorting:** Engineered a real-time search bar, category filter buttons (`All`, `Sealed TCG`, `Accessories`, `Board Games`), and price sorting (`Low to High`, `High to Low`) on `products.html` to dynamically filter DOM nodes without page reloads (Flanagan, 2020: 415).



## 4. Search Engine Optimization (SEO) & Security Implementation
On-Page SEO:** Unique, keyword-optimised `<title>`, `<meta name="description">`, and `<meta name="keywords">` tags were integrated into all five pages targeting local search intent in KwaZulu-Natal (Google Search Central, 2025).
Image Optimisation:** All `<img>` elements incorporate descriptive, hyphenated filenames (e.g., `pokemon-obsidian-flames-etb-kzn.jpg`), explicit `width`/`height` dimensions to prevent Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS), and keyword-rich `alt` attributes for screen readers (W3C, 2023).
Technical SEO (`robots.txt` & `sitemap.xml`):** Created a root-level `robots.txt` file instructing search engine crawlers to index all public pages and linked an XML sitemap (`sitemap.xml`) defining page priorities and update frequencies (Google Search Central, 2025).
Security & Page Speed:** Applied input sanitization in JavaScript to prevent Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) injection on form inputs, deferred script execution (`defer`), and utilised lazy loading (`loading="lazy"`) on catalogue imagery (MDN Web Docs, 2026b).



## 5. Form Validation, Processing & Email Compilation
Enquiry Form (`enquiry.html`):** Validates customer name, email format ( via Regular Expressions), South African phone numbers (`10 digits`), quantity/participants, and enquiry type. Upon validation, the script dynamically calculates and displays an **Instant Cost & Availability Quote** (e.g., calculating total ZAR cost for booster box pre-orders or tournament entry fees and checking live seat availability).
Contact Form (`contact.html`):** Validates sender credentials, subject category, target branch, and minimum message length with real-time inline error messages. Once validated, the script simulates an asynchronous AJAX submission and compiles the payload into a structured `mailto:` URI directed to the selected store branch (`pmb@kzncollectibles.co.za` or `hilton@kzncollectibles.co.za`).



